.TH BOSWAS-DEVICE 1 "October 2026" "boswas-device-agent 1.0~alpha3" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-device \- Boswas device identity, agent status, configuration and enrollment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-device
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-device
shows and controls the Boswas device agent
.RB ( boswas-device-agent.service ).
The agent keeps the device's persistent identity, its state and inventory,
serves the local management API used by the Boswas Compatibility Manager, and,
when a Boswas Control Plane is configured, talks to it over mutual TLS.
A device without a Control Plane works fully standalone.
.PP
Read-only commands work without the service; they then show the agent's last
published status and say so.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Device state (READY, DEGRADED, OFFLINE, UPDATING, ERROR, MAINTENANCE,
INITIALIZING), agent version, Control Plane connection and last contact,
applied policy, pending messages.
.TP
.B identity
The device ID (a random UUID created at the agent's first start), when and how
it was created, whether it is ephemeral (live session) and the certificate
fingerprint after enrollment.
.TP
.B "identity reset \-\-yes"
Create a new device identity (root; the device must be unenrolled).
.TP
.BR "config validate " [ \-\-file " \fIFILE\fR]"
Check
.I /etc/boswas/device.conf
(or another file). Exits 1 if it has errors.
.TP
.B config show
Effective settings.
.TP
.BR "inventory " [ \-\-refresh ]
The device inventory, exactly as it would be reported: OS, Boswas packages,
Windows applications (no user names) and, with INVENTORY_POLICY=standard,
CPU, memory, model and disk size. Never serial numbers or MAC addresses.
.TP
.B policy
The applied device policy and the effective WinCompat policy.
.TP
.BR "commands " [ \-\-limit " \fIN\fR]"
Remote commands received from the Control Plane and their outcome.
.TP
.BR "events " [ \-\-limit " \fIN\fR]"
The device event log.
.TP
.BR "enroll " [ \-\-token\-file " \fIFILE\fR]"
Enroll with the Control Plane set in
.I device.conf
(root). The one-time enrollment token is read from
.I FILE
or from standard input; it is never accepted on the command line and never
stored.
.TP
.B "unenroll \-\-yes"
Leave the Control Plane (root). The device forgets its certificate, the
managed policy and the managed catalog; the local WinCompat policy applies
again.
.TP
.B sync
Contact the Control Plane now (root).
.TP
.BR "maintenance on" | off
Pause or resume remote commands (root).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 failed, or
.B config validate
found errors; 2 usage error; 4 refused (root required or not permitted);
5 the device agent service is not running; 70 internal error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/boswas/device.conf
Device configuration (administrator; never secrets).
.TP
.I /var/lib/boswas/agent/
Agent state: identity.json, status.json, inventory.json (public); credentials,
policy, outbox and the command ledger (root only).
.TP
.I /run/boswas-agent/agent.sock
Local management API.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas (1),
.BR boswas-winapp (1),
.BR boswas-compat-manager (1)
